# Obsidian vault hybrid

- **Backend owns** IDs, types, timestamps, structured links, provenance, statuses, sync metadata. **Never** merge vault frontmatter or system zones into the DB as authoritative structural updates.
- **Write-back**: only content inside approved markers:

```text
<!-- editable:start:section-name -->
...
<!-- editable:end:section-name -->
```

- **Folder layout** (deterministic export): `00-dashboard`, `01-sources`, `02-evidence`, `03-claims`, `04-tensions`, `05-decisions`, `06-outputs`, `07-notes`, `08-templates`, `99-system` (see [docs/obsidian-sync.md](docs/obsidian-sync.md)).
- **Dashboard notes**: regenerated projections — treat as **read-only** in the vault workflow.
- **Freeform notes** (`07-notes` or equivalent): not canonical structured objects unless promoted through the app.
- **Conflicts**: explicit state on `SyncRecord`; hash export/import payloads (see `note-fingerprint` / sync lib). Do not silently overwrite local edits.

Implementation lives under [apps/web/src/lib/obsidian/](apps/web/src/lib/obsidian/); templates in [vault-templates/](vault-templates/).
